codex
The implementation passes its acceptance tests in a prepared environment, but the default CLI path breaks after a normal install and the emitted staleness rows are sorted contrary to the documented tier order. These are functional issues in the intended consumer workflow.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Load default tiers from the surveyed repo — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-32-sbom-code/scripts/sbom-survey/sbom_survey/survey.py:486-486
  When the tool is installed non-editably (for example `pip install scripts/sbom-survey`, which the README/.gitignore flow references), this default resolves to `site-packages/sbom_survey/tiers.toml`; `tiers.toml` is not packaged there, so `sbom-survey --repo . --offline` exits 1 with `FileNotFoundError` unless the caller passes `--tiers`. The default path needs to be derived from `repo_root` or the tier file needs to be included as package data.

- [P2] Sort rows by the ruled tier order — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-32-sbom-code/scripts/sbom-survey/sbom_survey/survey.py:184-185
  When the output contains both `shipped` and `dev-tooling` rows, sorting on the tier string puts `dev-tooling` before `shipped`, even though `TIER_VOCABULARY` and the documented staleness contract put `shipped` first. This makes the generated `staleness.json`/Markdown violate the ruled consumer order; use the tier rank rather than the raw string in the row sort key.
